cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, cite this software record and the scientific
  publications listed in the README.
type: software
title: "NEGF TDP PS-SCBA: Protocol-Conditioned Projected Stationary Transport"
version: 0.2.0
date-released: 2026-09-01
authors:
  - family-names: Rossignol
    given-names: Louis
  - family-names: Zhouyin
    given-names: Zhanghao
  - family-names: Guo
    given-names: Hong
repository-code: "https://github.com/louis-rsgl/NEGF-TDPSCBA"
abstract: >-
  Python implementation of protocol-conditioned projected stationary
  self-consistent Born approximation transport for a scalar electronic level
  with Lorentzian finite-bandwidth leads and one phonon mode. Downward, upward,
  and square voltage protocols are solved through an outer projected fixed
  point; preparation-fixed kernels remain available as a comparison baseline.
keywords:
  - nonequilibrium Green functions
  - time-dependent quantum transport
  - electron-phonon interaction
  - self-consistent Born approximation
  - finite-bandwidth leads
  - minimal pole representation
  - projected stationary approximation
